WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:18.276
Ben flew up to the photography classroom and tried to turn the doorknob.

2
00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:19.997
But the door was locked.

3
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:22.678
He knocked.

4
00:00:22.698 --> 00:00:25.398
"Pixel? Are you in there?

5
00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:26.859
It's me, Ben."

6
00:00:27.379 --> 00:00:30.880
There was no reply, so Ben floated through the door.

7
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:37.524
In the back of the classroom, he could see the small darkroom, once used for developing photographs.

8
00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:45.310
Sure enough, Pixel was huddled in a corner.

9
00:00:46.071 --> 00:00:48.552
He was hunched over something, sobbing.

10
00:00:55.858 --> 00:00:56.818
Are you okay?"

11
00:00:57.739 --> 00:00:58.640
Pixel jumped.

12
00:00:59.788 --> 00:01:03.951
Floating toward the younger ghost, Ben saw tears streaming down his face.

13
00:01:06.913 --> 00:01:07.574
"What happened?"

14
00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.634
Ben asked.

15
00:01:08.654 --> 00:01:10.115
"Did you see the vandal?

16
00:01:10.435 --> 00:01:10.996
Are you hurt?"

17
00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:16.220
Pixel stared at Ben, unable to speak for a moment.

18
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.863
"I'm okay," he finally said in a shaky voice.

19
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:22.364
"I'm not hurt."

20
00:01:22.384 --> 00:01:24.645
"Then what's wrong?"

21
00:01:25.046 --> 00:01:25.966
Ben asked again.

22
00:01:25.986 --> 00:01:28.248
"Look. I found your camera.

23
00:01:28.652 --> 00:01:29.973
Do you know who the vandal is?"

24
00:01:29.993 --> 00:01:35.217
"Yes, it's Pixel swallowed hard.

25
00:01:35.237 --> 00:01:38.340
"Me!" "What?"

26
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.242
Ben blinked in surprise.

27
00:01:40.262 --> 00:01:43.324
"You? You're the vandal?

28
00:01:43.764 --> 00:01:48.428
But He looked around and spotted the other two missing paintings.

29
00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:51.551
Their frames were broken too.

30
00:01:57.295 --> 00:02:00.181
wow." Ben ran a hand through his hair.

31
00:02:00.201 --> 00:02:01.462
"This is bad."

32
00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.123
He dropped into a chair.

33
00:02:04.143 --> 00:02:09.746
"I messed the paintings up," Pixel said.

34
00:02:09.766 --> 00:02:11.367
"I didn't steal them.

35
00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:13.388
And now I'm trying to fix them.

36
00:02:13.808 --> 00:02:15.049
Please believe me, Ben.

37
00:02:15.369 --> 00:02:17.430
I didn't mean for any of this to happen!"

38
00:02:18.291 --> 00:02:19.351
Ben shook his head.

39
00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.093
"Sorry, Pixel, but I don't understand."

40
00:02:23.294 --> 00:02:27.296
Pixel took a deep breath, and then the whole story tumbled out.

41
00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:30.853
"I wanted to get great photos for your article.

42
00:02:32.094 --> 00:02:35.835
So I tried to float in cool ways to get interesting angles.

43
00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.277
But I am not good at advanced floating techniques.

44
00:02:40.978 --> 00:02:43.899
I kept smashing into things—like Mr.

45
00:02:43.979 --> 00:02:45.099
Freaky's sculpture.

46
00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.401
I bashed into the motor and made the whole thing go haywire!"

47
00:02:49.421 --> 00:02:54.463
"Okay," Ben said slowly.

48
00:02:54.483 --> 00:02:56.124
"What else did you do?"

49
00:02:59.228 --> 00:03:01.449
"I knocked over all the artwork too!

50
00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:07.853
But I didn't want anyone to know, so I grabbed the three broken paintings and brought them to

51
00:03:07.873 --> 00:03:09.113
the newspaper office.

52
00:03:09.914 --> 00:03:11.995
I tried to fix them, but I couldn't.

53
00:03:13.015 --> 00:03:15.337
That's when I made those dumb copies.

54
00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:23.681
I was hoping nobody would notice."

55
00:03:24.261 --> 00:03:25.382
Pixel made a face.

56
00:03:25.402 --> 00:03:27.383
"Pretty dumb, huh?"

57
00:03:27.403 --> 00:03:30.428
"Nope." Ben frowned.

58
00:03:30.448 --> 00:03:32.389
"Very dumb!"

59
00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:34.410
Pixel winced.

60
00:03:35.711 --> 00:03:38.492
"That explains the painting in the newspaper office closet.

61
00:03:38.972 --> 00:03:39.992
By the way, Mr.

62
00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.673
Freaky found it and blamed me!"

63
00:03:41.693 --> 00:03:47.155
"Sorry." The younger ghost winced again.

64
00:03:47.175 --> 00:03:53.278
"I was working on it in there, and somebody came in, so I shoved it into the closet.

65
00:03:55.119 --> 00:03:58.380
Every time I tried to go back for it, somebody was in the office."

66
00:04:00.716 --> 00:04:02.036
"What about the flying painting?"

67
00:04:02.337 --> 00:04:03.057
Ben asked.

68
00:04:03.077 --> 00:04:05.157
"That got vandalized twice."

69
00:04:06.938 --> 00:04:09.299
"I knocked over the paints earlier in the week.

70
00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:19.482
And then today I smeared the paint while I was trying to take photos.

71
00:04:20.302 --> 00:04:23.243
I didn't realize the flying painting was still wet!"

72
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.364
"Go on."

73
00:04:27.904 --> 00:04:33.088
"While I was trying to sneak out of the gym without being noticed, I dropped my camera.

74
00:04:33.648 --> 00:04:35.530
I couldn't go back for it because Mr.

75
00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:36.631
Gwarg was in there."

76
00:04:39.393 --> 00:04:40.293
Pixel shrugged.

77
00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:43.335
"I'm just so awful at floating!

78
00:04:43.856 --> 00:04:47.479
I know I should practice more often, but I like photography better.

79
00:04:48.119 --> 00:04:52.042
I'd much rather take pictures than practice boring floating techniques."

80
00:04:52.062 --> 00:04:54.744
"Wow. Pixel."

81
00:04:55.244 --> 00:04:58.005
Ben sat there for a minute with his chin in his hands.

82
00:04:59.025 --> 00:05:03.006
He couldn't believe how much damage Pixel had caused—all by mistake.

83
00:05:03.026 --> 00:05:07.467
"Why didn't he ask me or a teacher for help?"

84
00:05:07.947 --> 00:05:08.568
Ben thought.

85
00:05:09.548 --> 00:05:13.209
But of course Ben knew the answer to that question perfectly well.

86
00:05:13.229 --> 00:05:18.710
"I used to have trouble with floating too," Ben blurted out.

87
00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:24.072
"For the longest time, I couldn't float through doors and walls.

88
00:05:24.796 --> 00:05:26.557
I was too embarrassed to tell anyone."

89
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:30.077
Pixel blinked at him.

90
00:05:30.097 --> 00:05:32.878
"Really? Same as me?"

91
00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:36.599
"Yep. But I practiced and I got better.

92
00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.360
You can do that too."

93
00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.081
"I'll try, I promise.

94
00:05:42.981 --> 00:05:45.702
But Tears filled Pixel's eyes again.

95
00:05:45.722 --> 00:05:49.103
"In the meantime I ruined Art Week!"

96
00:05:49.603 --> 00:05:50.463
He shook his head.

97
00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:54.104
"Worst of all, I wrecked the witches' beautiful painting."

98
00:05:55.432 --> 00:05:57.934
"Art Week isn't over yet," Ben said.

99
00:05:57.954 --> 00:06:00.857
"And the witches are very good artists.

100
00:06:01.517 --> 00:06:03.379
They're fixing the flying painting right now."

101
00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.442
He glanced at the artwork on the floor near Pixel.

102
00:06:07.462 --> 00:06:12.947
"It looks like you've finished repairing those paintings, so we can hang them back up in the hallway."

103
00:06:14.048 --> 00:06:16.410
Pixel nodded as he wiped away his tears.

104
00:06:17.131 --> 00:06:19.893
Then he glanced up at a clock on the darkroom wall.

105
00:06:19.913 --> 00:06:22.996
"I guess we'd better hurry, Ben.

106
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.902
Leonardo da Creepy will be here any minute!"

107
00:06:25.922 --> 00:06:29.185
"Yeah," Ben said with a grin.

108
00:06:29.205 --> 00:06:33.328
"And we need to get your photos ready for my newspaper article!"
